            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a brake, then the Telugu for a horn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఇంధనం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇంధనం — indhanaṁ — \"fuel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దారి మధ్యలో కారులో ఇంధనం అయిపోయింది. dāri madhyalō kārulō indhanaṁ ayipōyindi. Halfway there the car ran out of fuel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word for every kind of fuel: firewood, petrol, gas. అయిపోవు, to run out, goes with it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇంధనం (indhanaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit indhana, \"lighting, kindling, fuel\", from the root indh, \"to kindle\" (CDIAL 1584)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
