        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చెడిపోవు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడిపోవు — ceḍipōvu — \"to break down; to go bad\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దారిలో మా బస్సు చెడిపోయింది. dārilō mā bassu ceḍipōyindi. Our bus broke down on the way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): చెడిపోయింది, ceḍipōyindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడు, bad, + పోవు, to go: gone bad. A machine breaks down this way, and food goes off this way too. Its subject is a thing, so the past shown is the third person: చెడిపోయింది, it broke down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడిపోవు (ceḍipōvu) is native Dravidian: చెడు, \"to rot, to be spoiled\" (DEDR 2760), with పోవు, \"to go\" (DEDR 4572), which marks a change that has happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
